<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Lydenburg</h1><p class="st-meta">1856 CE – 1860 CE · capital Lydenburg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A breakaway Boer republic in the eastern Transvaal that resisted union with Pretoria for four years.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/voortrekkers">Voortrekkers</a> abandoned malaria-ridden <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohrigstad">Andries-Ohrigstad</a> and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydenburg">Lydenburg</a> in 1849. Its leaders distrusted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marthinus-wessel-pretorius">Marthinus Wessel Pretorius</a> and the western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/south-african-republic">Transvaal</a>, and in 1856 the Lydenburg community declared itself a separate republic, De Republiek Lydenburg in Zuid-Afrika.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The small republic had its own <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volksraad">Volksraad</a> and a church tradition closer to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-reformed-church">Dutch Reformed</a> establishment of the Cape. Its farmers lived from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>, hunting and trade towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delagoa-bay">Delagoa Bay</a>, and lived alongside the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pedi-kingdom">Pedi Kingdom</a> to the west, with whom relations were uneasy.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydenburg">Lydenburg</a> absorbed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-utrecht">Republic of Utrecht</a> in 1858, and in 1860 the combined state rejoined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/south-african-republic">South African Republic</a>. The town remained a district centre and later a base in wars against the Pedi.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-lydenburg.jpg" alt="Republic of Lydenburg" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Netherlands.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1856 CE – 1860 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lydenburg</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Dutch Reformed Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/south-africa">South Africa</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lydenburg Republic, De Republiek Lydenburg in Zuid-Afrika</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1858&amp;focus=republic-of-lydenburg" aria-label="Republic of Lydenburg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5488 3101 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Lydenburg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5808 3357L5796 3447M5808 3357L5746 3380"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5796 3447h0M5746 3380h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5808 3357h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5808 3357h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Lydenburg. <a href="/atlas?year=1858&amp;focus=republic-of-lydenburg">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
